From e7867a09dc78f72cc0f72496df136f93822fe286 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:43:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Benchmark of the linear solvers of the factory on assembled
 systems

LinearSolversBenchmark (benchmarks/, option BENCHMARKS, parallel builds)
measures any linear solver of the factory, its parameters being given on
the command line in a small text syntax, on the Laplace equation on a
cube or on the linear elasticity of a cantilever beam, possibly with
stiff cubic inclusions, the unknowns being ordered by nodes or by vector
dimension. It prints the times of the setup, of the first resolution
(some preconditioners are built at their first application), of the
following resolutions and of the setup and resolution of a second
operator of the same sparsity, the number of iterations, the residuals
and the convergence reported.
